{"step_index":4084,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T22:17:59Z","thinking":"Reviewing the previous session's summary for Cure Pharma, specifically the details within `scratch/inspect_newest_results.py`. This includes noting the 12 matches and the two review entries, particularly the pharmaceutical name and strength mappings.\n\n\nThe system's \"no_match\" classification for \"باروفين 30قرص\" appears to stem from a stricter interpretation of package size discrepancies within a larger batch, despite explicitly identifying it as a \"review\" case individually. The model correctly identifies the name and form match, but the differing tablet counts (30 vs. 20) lead to the incorrect classification. This highlights a need to refine the system to apply \"review\" consistently even when the number differs.\n\n\nComparing the previous run's results (before yesterday's fixes) to the current one, the initial audit shows a significant shift. The previous run had 71 matched items, but with several critical errors, and a concerning 140 items flagged for review.\n\nCurrently, the goal is to evaluate the improvements in matching accuracy, the reduction in review cases, and identify any persistent false negatives, specifically those existing in the inventory but overlooked. This will include an in-depth check of the \"matched\" category for the elimination of those known errors.\n\n\nA substantial improvement is confirmed: the system now achieves 72 matches across six warehouses with a drastic 96% reduction in review items (from 140 to 6). Brand identity and form integrity are also significantly improved, resolving the previous false positives and form-mismatches. The 6 remaining items requiring review appear to be genuine pack size discrepancies of the same drug and strength.\nThe match distribution across warehouses is: السلام شبين (19), المكرومي المنصورة (17), كيور فارما خاص (12), مخزن الحياة فارم اسكندريه-170 (6), جملة العمروووو (1), and الهضبة الاثنين نقدى0 (17). The first review item is Doliprane 1000mg tablets, with a size difference between the requested and the stored package (15 vs 60 tablets).\n\n\nExamining the detailed discrepancies in the remaining \"review\" cases reveals pack size as the consistent differentiating factor. \"Genuphil\", \"Triplixam\", and \"Averocoxib\" discrepancies are all due to differing tablet counts. \"Averocoxib\" also shows inventory entry inconsistencies (single tablets vs. standard pack sizes). \"Dancet\" shows a vial count difference. These observations inform a targeted refinement to the matching algorithm.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"import openpyxl\\n\\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook(r'data/processes/PROC-001/results_PROC-001.xlsx', data_only=True)\\nfor sheet in wb.sheetnames:\\n    if sheet not in ['ملخص', 'لم يُعثر عليه', 'يحتاج مراجعة']:\\n        ws = wb[sheet]\\n        rows = list(ws.iter_rows(values_only=True))[1:]\\n        print(f\\\"\\\\n==================== {sheet} ({len(rows)} matches) ====================\\\")\\n        for i, r in enumerate(rows, 1):\\n            print(f\\\"{i:2d}. المطلوب: '{r[0]}'  <===>  المخزن: '{r[1]}' [{r[2]}]\\\")\\n\"","Description":"\"Print all 72 matches across all warehouse sheets\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"d:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\Pharmacy-agy\\\\scratch\\\\print_all_72_matches.py\"","toolAction":"\"Write print script\"","toolSummary":"\"Print all 72 matches\""}}]}
